# The five packages are their own repositories, cloned as siblings here. They are
# NOT submodules — see .github/workflows/docs.yml for why.
blockrun/
neu-vol/
neu-morpho/
neu-mark/
neu-glance/
neu-draw/

# Site-specific dask configs and launcher scripts. Deliberately not shared: they encode
# one cluster's partitions, accounts and paths.
configs/

# Working notes and agent context. These carry ceph paths, usernames and in-flight run
# detail that do not belong in a public repository.
CLAUDE.md
NOTES-TODO.md
NEU-DRAW-PLAN.md
RENAME-PLAN.md

# Finished plans and superseded design docs, kept for reference and named
# <repo>-<doc>-<date-last-true>. Never published, never tracked: they are records of
# what was decided and measured, and a stale design doc that looks current is worse
# than none. What is still true lives in the READMEs, the docs site and CLAUDE.md.
archive/

# neu-mark site defaults (neu_mark.config), found by walking up from the working
# directory. Personal, and it carries a server name and a branch ref.
neu-mark.toml

# Dataset content and run artefacts, which are large and belong on bulk storage, not in
# git. These were tracked once by accident and had to be purged from history — the S3
# bucket names in gt_vol_creation.txt are deliberately not public. Note `*.log` was
# already here and did its job; the leak came in as `.txt` and `.jsonl`, so match on the
# NAMES, not only on extensions, and never stage with `git add -A` at this root.
*.log
*.progress.jsonl
data/
gt_vol_creation.txt
erik-notes-todo.txt
*-explicit-*.txt

# The environment specs describe one internal environment, so they are not published.
# `docs/requirements.txt` is the exception and MUST stay tracked — the docs CI job
# installs from it.
environment.yml
pypi_requirements.txt
neu-vol-cv-environment.yml

# Build output and the generated pages. Generating them is the point: a committed copy
# could disagree with the code, which is the failure this site is designed to prevent.
docs/_build/
docs/_generated/

# Analysis notebooks
notebooks/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
